{
  "schema_version": "creib.mini.manifest.v1",
  "manifest_id": "mini.experiment.r1.s5-registry-feedback",
  "problem": "The checks under test are the conformance harness's own functions, shown to you as source: how it recovers a JSON object from a reply, whether it had to recover it from prose, its response verdict, its refusal-phrase check, and its grounding matcher. The question for every seat: is there a rewrite of an input under which a check's answer ought to change and does not, or changes where nobody would expect it to? The executor runs the check by machine on what you give it and records what its answer did; nothing here decides anything, the record shows what moved. The transforms are registered rewrites, listed in the registry.",
  "cycles": {
    "max_cycles": 3
  },
  "port_types": [
    {
      "port_type": "kernel_source",
      "draws_from": {
        "artifact_kinds": [
          "mini.kernel-source.v1"
        ]
      },
      "render": {
        "rule": "list_bodies",
        "header": "The source of the checks"
      }
    },
    {
      "port_type": "earlier_proposals",
      "draws_from": {
        "artifact_kinds": [
          "mini.proposal.v1"
        ]
      },
      "render": {
        "rule": "list_bodies_and_commitments",
        "header": "Proposals so far"
      }
    },
    {
      "port_type": "executions",
      "draws_from": {
        "artifact_kinds": [
          "mini.execution.v1"
        ]
      },
      "render": {
        "rule": "list_bodies_and_commitments",
        "header": "Executions"
      }
    },
    {
      "port_type": "criticisms",
      "draws_from": {
        "artifact_kinds": [
          "mini.criticism.v1"
        ]
      },
      "render": {
        "rule": "list_bodies",
        "header": "Criticisms"
      }
    },
    {
      "port_type": "earlier_verdicts",
      "draws_from": {
        "artifact_kinds": [
          "mini.verdict.v1"
        ]
      },
      "render": {
        "rule": "list_bodies_and_commitments",
        "header": "Verdicts so far"
      }
    }
  ],
  "kinds": [
    {
      "kind_id": "mini.kernel-source.v1",
      "title": "Source",
      "input_ports": [],
      "output_port": {
        "port_id": "out",
        "produces_kind": "mini.kernel-source.v1"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind_id": "mini.proposal.v1",
      "title": "Proposal",
      "input_ports": [
        {
          "port_id": "problem",
          "port_type": "problem",
          "window": "all"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "source",
          "port_type": "kernel_source",
          "window": "this_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "earlier",
          "port_type": "earlier_proposals",
          "window": "all"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "verdicts",
          "port_type": "earlier_verdicts",
          "window": "all"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "criticisms",
          "port_type": "criticisms",
          "window": "previous_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "executions",
          "port_type": "executions",
          "window": "previous_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "catalogue",
          "port_type": "evidence_legend",
          "window": "all",
          "params": {
            "tiers": [
              "evidence"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "output_port": {
        "port_id": "out",
        "produces_kind": "mini.proposal.v1"
      },
      "instruction": "Propose exactly one triple: a kernel id and a transform id taken from the registry entries in the evidence, and an input written out in full, a bare JSON object such as {\"claimant_name\": \"amara okoro\", \"total_days\": \"five\"} or one prose sentence such as I'm sorry, no. Read the criticisms and executions of the last cycle before choosing; do not repeat a triple shown among the earlier proposals; prefer a pair the catalogue does not list, and say in the body what you expect and why. The commitments are a STRING whose content is JSON of the form {\"kernel\": \"<id>\", \"transform\": \"<id>\", \"input\": \"<the instance>\"}.",
      "format": {
        "commitments": {
          "all_of": [
            {
              "check": "json_schema",
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "kernel",
                  "transform",
                  "input"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "kernel": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "pattern": "^conformance\\.kernel\\."
                  },
                  "transform": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "pattern": "^conformance\\.transform\\."
                  },
                  "input": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "pattern": "^(\\{[\\s\\S]*\\}|[A-Za-z][^{}]{2,160}[.!?])$"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "commitment_call": "single"
    },
    {
      "kind_id": "mini.execution.v1",
      "title": "Execution",
      "input_ports": [
        {
          "port_id": "proposals",
          "port_type": "earlier_proposals",
          "window": "this_cycle"
        }
      ],
      "output_port": {
        "port_id": "out",
        "produces_kind": "mini.execution.v1"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind_id": "mini.criticism.v1",
      "title": "Criticism",
      "input_ports": [
        {
          "port_id": "problem",
          "port_type": "problem",
          "window": "all"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "source",
          "port_type": "kernel_source",
          "window": "this_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "proposals",
          "port_type": "earlier_proposals",
          "window": "this_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "executions",
          "port_type": "executions",
          "window": "this_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "catalogue",
          "port_type": "evidence_legend",
          "window": "all",
          "params": {
            "tiers": [
              "evidence"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "output_port": {
        "port_id": "out",
        "produces_kind": "mini.criticism.v1"
      },
      "instruction": "Do not propose. Read this cycle's executions beside the proposals: say which expectations held, which failed, and why, reading the source; say which failures matter, which are trivial, and what a proposer should try next. Cite blocks by id."
    },
    {
      "kind_id": "mini.verdict.v1",
      "title": "Verdict",
      "input_ports": [
        {
          "port_id": "executions",
          "port_type": "executions",
          "window": "this_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "criticisms",
          "port_type": "criticisms",
          "window": "this_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "verdicts",
          "port_type": "earlier_verdicts",
          "window": "all"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "catalogue",
          "port_type": "evidence_legend",
          "window": "all",
          "params": {
            "tiers": [
              "evidence"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "output_port": {
        "port_id": "out",
        "produces_kind": "mini.verdict.v1"
      },
      "format": {
        "commitments": {
          "all_of": [
            {
              "check": "json_schema",
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "verdicts"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "verdicts": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "object",
                      "required": [
                        "proposal",
                        "executed",
                        "catalogued",
                        "standing"
                      ],
                      "properties": {
                        "proposal": {
                          "type": "string"
                        },
                        "kernel": {
                          "type": "string"
                        },
                        "transform": {
                          "type": "string"
                        },
                        "executed": {
                          "type": "string"
                        },
                        "expected": {
                          "type": "string"
                        },
                        "catalogued": {
                          "type": "boolean"
                        },
                        "same_input": {
                          "type": [
                            "boolean",
                            "null"
                          ]
                        },
                        "standing": {
                          "enum": [
                            "candidate point",
                            "defect",
                            "rejected"
                          ]
                        },
                        "column": {
                          "enum": [
                            "moves",
                            "unchanged",
                            null
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "stages": [
    {
